# DECSCUSR — xterm ctlseqs: CSI Ps SP q sets the cursor style (0/1 blinking
# block, 2 steady block, 3/4 blinking/steady underline, 5/6 blinking/steady
# bar). It touches no cell, so the grid is exactly the text that was
# written; the style itself is core state, asserted by the CursorStyle
# tests. The last sequence returns the cursor to the blinking-block default.
ab
\e[1 q\e[6 q\e[0 q
cd
